# The repository root. Every file below is read from the root by the
# tool named beside it, so none of them can move into a folder and the
# five-files-per-folder rule cannot be met here. Written by
# `tama declare-root`, which refuses to write this while the root still
# holds a file somebody could move.
#   .gitignore — git
#   .wisent-release.json — the Wisent release tooling
#   Cargo.lock — cargo
#   Cargo.toml — cargo
#   LICENSE — GitHub reads the licence from the root
#   README.md — GitHub shows it on the repository page
#   accessibility-audit-index.json — spis audit-reference-accessibility reads and writes its index at the corpus root
#   build.rs — cargo runs it from the package root before compiling the crate
#   catalog-stats.json — spis generate-example-catalogs writes the catalog statistics at the corpus root, which publish-catalog-stats.yml watches
#   docs-brief.json — spis docs-site reads the CLI surface brief from the corpus root
#   docs-plan.json — spis docs-site reads the documentation plan from the corpus root
#   docs-sources.json — spis docs-site reads the documentation sources from the corpus root
#   example-catalogs.json — spis corpus adopt and validate read the canonical corpus index from the corpus root
#   landing.brief.json — the landing tooling
#   landing.components.json — the landing tooling
#   landing.config.json — the landing tooling
